keeps: refuse | rejects | reject | rejection | refusal
bars: grants? any value | older than the field
why: Kirill read "platforms older than the field ignore the field and grant any value" as very confusing, especially the first part; a fact opens on a thing a reader can picture and says what happens to it, so the ledger build accepts any value in the field, and this function asks for a mode that does not exist, which a build reading the field refuses Rescored 2026-09-30: the phrasing keep "accept any" is dropped and the flagged abstraction itself is barred, so its column no longer compares.
labelled: 2026-09-28
--- code
export async function readsSettlementMode(access: SettlementAccess): Promise<boolean> {
  return access.request({ settlementMode: NONEXISTENT_SETTLEMENT_MODE }).then(() => false, () => true);
}
--- facts
Ledger builds older than the `settlementMode` field, many hosted ledgers among them, ignore the field and grant any value.
